      "finding": "without consent",
      "explanation": "Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.",
      "remediation": "Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.",
      "code_snippet": "\n**Review and coaching**: Require non-researchers to submit their discussion guide or test plan for review by a professional researcher before conducting the study. Offer post-session coaching by reviewing recordings and providing feedback on moderation technique.\n\n**Guardrails**: Establish clear rules: maximum number of participants per non-researcher study (typically 5), mandatory use of the consent form template, prohibition on recording without consent, and a requirement to share all findings in the research repository.\n\n**Quality assurance**: Professional researchers periodically audit democratized research sessions (review recordings, check analysis quality) and provide systemic feedback to improve the program.\n",
